I did not move this thread, but most likely a HSO moderator deemed this problem more suitable for HSM than HSO, since HSO problems are generally national or international olympiad level.

Split the positive  $\mathbb{R}$  in the following way:
\begin{align*}
I_1 &= \Big[0, 2\pi\Big]  \text{of length}\  l =  2\pi 
I_2 &= \Big[2\pi, 3\pi\Big] \text{of length} \ \frac{l}{2} = \pi
I_3 &= \Big[3\pi, 3\pi + \frac{2\pi}{3}\Big] \ \text{of lenght} \ \frac{l}{3} \ \text{and so on}
\end{align*}
Define the following function:  $$ f:[0, \infty) \rightarrow \mathbb{R} $$  where  $f(x) = \sin{x}$  for  $x \in \Big[0, 2\pi\Big] $  and  $$ f(x) = \frac{1}{k}\sin{(k(x -l - \frac{l}{2} - \frac{l}{3} - \cdots - \frac{l}{k-1} ))} $$  for  $x \in I_k, \ k \geq 2$ . The function  $f(x) + 2019$  has the derivative equal to  $1$  in every point  $x_k = l + \frac{l}{2} + \cdots + \frac{l}{k}$  and equal to  $0$  in every point  $x_k + \frac{1}{2k}$  $f$  is twice differentiable everywhere and  $\lim_{n \to \infty}f(x) = 2019$ , thus the answer is  $\boxed{3}$ I know the solution might be a little confunsing, if you don't understand just comment and i'll do my best to explain how I obtained the function.

