\frac{1}{a_k + 1} = \frac{a_k-1}{a_k^2 - 1}&= \frac{a_k+1-2}{a_k^2 - 1}
&= \frac{1}{a_k - 1} - \frac{2}{a_k^2 - 1} = \frac{1}{a_k-1} - \frac{1}{a_{k+1} -1}.
\end{align*}

Thus \[\sum_{j=1}^{N} \frac{1}{a_j + 1} = \frac{1}{2-1} - \frac{1}{a_N -1} = 1 - \frac{1}{a_N-1}<1 \qquad\blacksquare\]

