<details><summary>Solution</summary>We use the following trig formulae \begin{align}
OD&=R\cos ADH&=2R\cdot \cos^2B=2R\cdot\sin^2\left(\tfrac{A}{2}\right)=R(1-\cos A)
r&=4R\cdot \sin\left(\tfrac{A}{2}\right)\cdot\sin^2\left(\tfrac{B}{2}\right)
\end{align}
A condition of the problem is equivalent to
\begin{align*}46R\cdot\sin^2\left(\tfrac{A}{2}\right)=2R\cos A&\iff 23\cdot\sin^2\left(\tfrac{A}{2}\right)=\cos^2\left(\tfrac{A}{2}\right)-\sin^2\left(\tfrac{A}{2} \right)
&\iff 25\sin^2\left(\tfrac{A}{2}\right)=1\implies\cos A=\tfrac{23}{25}
\end{align*}
Now we have
\begin{align*}
    OD=\tfrac{23R}{25}\quad \text{and} \quad HD=\tfrac{2R}{25}\implies GD=\tfrac{16R}{25}
\end{align*}
Finally we show  $r=\tfrac{8R}{25}$  which we equate with formula  $(3)$  to simplify to   $$ \sin^2\left(\tfrac{B}{2}\right)=\tfrac{2}{5}\iff \cos B=\frac{1}{5} $$   which is true and we have  $GI=ID=r$ , so we are done. :yoda:</details>
