Let  $a=da_0$ ,  $b=db_0$ , with  $\gcd(a_0,b_0)=1$ . We have  $da_0+1\mid d+da_0b_0$ , or that  $\gcd(d+da_0b_0,da_0+1)=da_0+1$ . Note that \begin{align*}
    \gcd(d+da_0b_0,da_0+1) &= \gcd(1+a_0b_0, da_0+1) 
    &= \gcd(a_0(b_0-d),da_0+1) 
    &= \gcd(b_0-d, da_0+1).
\end{align*}
Suppose, FTSOC, that  $b_0\ne d$ . Then,  $b_0-d \ge da_0+1$ , implying  $b_0 \ge a_0(d+1)+1 > a_0$ , absurd. Thus,  $b_0=d$ , and  $b = d^2$ , as desired.  $\blacksquare$

