\begin{align*}
\sqrt{x^2 + 5} + \sqrt{y^2 + 5} &= 6  
x + y &= 4 
\end{align*}
But to solve this, we just note that
\begin{align*}
36 &= (\sqrt{x^2 + 5} + \sqrt{y^2 + 5})^2  
&= (x^2 + 5) + (y^2 + 5) + 2 \sqrt{(x^2 + 5)(y^2 + 5)}  
&\stackrel{\text{CS}}{\ge} (x^2 + 5) + (y^2 + 5) + 2(xy + 5) = (x + y)^2 + 20 = 36 
\end{align*}
and as equality hold, we must have  $x = y = 2$  and thus  $a = b = 9$  as desired.

